# Marine Eco System

An HTML5-only, five-page website created from the Marine Eco Eco sytsem proposal. It presents the business, promotes its technology services and gives customers ways to submit inquiries, quotation requests and booking requests.

## Pages

- `index.html` — Home page and service overview
- `about.html` — Business history, mission, vision, values and target audience
- `service.html` —Coastal & Beach Cleanups,Wildlife Rehabilitation Support, Wildlife Rehabilitation Support<
- `inquiry.html` — Inquiry, Enquiry Category  and booking request form
- `contact.html` — Contact information, hours and contact form

## Folder structure

```text
Kasi_Tech/
├── index.html
├── about.html
├── service.html
├── inquiry.html
├── contact.html
├── README.md
├── CHANGELOG.md
└── images/
    ├── Costal Cleanups.jpg
    ├── ecosystem.jpg
    ├── Penguin.jpg
    ├── Gear Safety.jpg

    
```

## How to run

1. Extract the `Assigment 1 Part 1 A.Ngcamla`  ZIP file.
2. Open the `Marine Eco System` folder.
3. Double-click `index.html`, or open it using a web browser.
4. Use the navigation menu to visit all five pages.

No installation, server, CSS or JavaScript is required.

## Important setup before publishing

The proposal did not include confirmed business contact details. Search all HTML files and replace:

- `+27 00 000 0000` with the correct telephone number.
- `Marine_Eco.co.za` with the active business email address.
- `[Insert street address]`, `[Insert suburb]` and `[Insert city]` with the physical address.
- The example operating hours if the business follows a different schedule.

## Forms

The inquiry and contact forms use HTML validation and submission. When a visitor submits a form, the browser opens the visitor's configured email application. A hosted production website should later connect these forms to a secure server-side form handler or database.

## HTML validation

Validate every page using the official W3C Markup Validation Service: <https://validator.w3.org/>

## Version control

Suggested first Git commands:

```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Create initial Marine Eco System HTML website"
git branch -M main
```

Create an empty GitHub repository, then follow GitHub's instructions to add the remote URL and push the `main` branch.

