# Marine Eco System

**Algoa Bay Marine Conservation Trust**  
A community-focused marine conservation website dedicated to protecting the biodiversity of Algoa Bay and Nelson Mandela Bay, Gqeberha, South Africa.

---

## About the Project

Marine Eco System is a static multi-page website created to raise awareness and encourage community involvement in marine conservation. The organisation was founded in 2018 by local marine biologists in Gqeberha to protect coastal ecosystems and endangered African Penguin populations.

The website provides information about the Trust’s mission, services, and ways for the public to get involved through volunteering, donations, educational programmes, and guided eco-tours.

---

## Features

- **Home Page** – Introduction to the organisation and featured marine projects  
- **About Page** – History, Mission Statement, and Vision Statement  
- **Services Page** – Overview of the main conservation programmes:
  - Coastal & Beach Cleanups
  - Wildlife Rehabilitation Support
  - Community Education & Outreach
- **Enquiry Page** – Detailed form for volunteer sign-ups, donations, tours, and general enquiries  
- **Contact Us Page** – Headquarters details, opening hours, Google Maps embed, and contact form  
- Responsive design for desktop, tablet, and mobile devices  
- Consistent header navigation and multi-column footer across all pages  
- Newsletter subscription section in the footer  

---

## Tech Stack

- HTML5  
- CSS3 (with CSS Variables / Custom Properties)  
- Responsive layout using Flexbox and CSS Grid  
- Google Maps Embed  
- SVG social media icons  

No JavaScript frameworks or backend are required — this is a pure front-end static website.

---

## Project Structure

```
Marine-Eco-System/
├── index.html                  # Home page
├── pages/
│   ├── about.html              # About page (History, Mission, Vision)
│   ├── services.html           # Services page
│   ├── enquiry.html            # Enquiry / Get Involved form
│   └── contactus.html          # Contact Us page
├── css/
│   └── style.css               # Main stylesheet
├── images/
│   ├── WEDDE LOGO.png          # Organisation logo
│   ├── ecosystem copy.jpg
│   ├── Penguin.jpg
│   └── Gear Safety.jpg
├── _shared.css                 # Shared styles (if used)
└── README.md                   # Project documentation
```

> **Note:** Some pages currently reference `../_shared.css` and `../css/style.css`. Adjust paths according to your final folder structure.

---

## How to View the Website

1. Download or clone the project folder.
2. Open `index.html` in any modern web browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari).
3. Navigate between pages using the main menu.

No server or build tools are required.

